    <div class="section">
        <h2>Key Hardening Measures Applied</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Password Policy:</strong> Maximum age 90 days, minimum length 14 characters</li>
            <li><strong>Account Lockout:</strong> 5 failed attempts lock account for 15 minutes</li>
            <li><strong>SSH Hardening:</strong> Key-based authentication, root login restricted, weak ciphers disabled</li>
            <li><strong>Firewall:</strong> Firewalld enabled with default zone configuration</li>
            <li><strong>Auditing:</strong> Auditd configured with critical operation tracking</li>
            <li><strong>Logging:</strong> Rsyslog configured for centralized logging</li>
            <li><strong>File Permissions:</strong> System files secured (passwd, shadow, SSH config)</li>
            <li><strong>Kernel Hardening:</strong> ASLR enabled, core dumps disabled, ptrace restricted</li>
            <li><strong>Services:</strong> Unnecessary services disabled, essential services enabled</li>
            <li><strong>SELinux:</strong> Configured in enforcing mode</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Critical Configurations</h2>
        <div class="control pass">
            <h4>✓ SSH Configuration Hardened</h4>
            <p>SSH daemon hardened with strong ciphers, key authentication required, root login restricted</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control pass">
            <h4>✓ Auditd Enabled</h4>
            <p>Audit daemon configured to track critical operations, identity changes, and system administration</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control pass">
            <h4>✓ Firewall Active</h4>
            <p>Firewalld configured and enabled with appropriate zone configuration</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control pass">
            <h4>✓ Kernel Hardening Applied</h4>
            <p>ASLR enabled, unprivileged BPF disabled, ptrace scope restricted</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control review">
            <h4>⚠ Review Required</h4>
            <p>Audit reports generated for world-writable files, SUID/SGID permissions, and network listeners</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Post-Hardening Recommendations</h2>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Verify SSH Access:</strong> Test SSH connectivity after hardening</li>
            <li><strong>Review Firewall Rules:</strong> Add application-specific firewall rules as needed</li>
            <li><strong>Validate Services:</strong> Confirm critical services are running properly</li>
            <li><strong>Check Logs:</strong> Review /var/log/secure and /var/log/audit/audit.log for errors</li>
            <li><strong>Configure SSH Keys:</strong> Implement key-based authentication exclusively</li>
            <li><strong>Set Up Log Forwarding:</strong> Consider centralized logging for security monitoring</li>
            <li><strong>Regular Backups:</strong> Maintain backup procedures for system configuration</li>
            <li><strong>Continuous Monitoring:</strong> Enable real-time security monitoring and alerting</li>
            <li><strong>Compliance Testing:</strong> Re-run validation playbooks periodically</li>
            <li><strong>Security Updates:</strong> Subscribe to security updates and apply promptly</li>
        </ol>
